  "id": "psychological-contract",
  "term": "psychological contract",
  "definition": "A psychological contract is the employee’s perceived relationship of mutual expectations and obligations between themselves and their organization. In this source, it is treated as part of the social exchange that shapes organizational commitment and may be reconstructed when work arrangements, such as co-working, change traditional organizational boundaries.",
